          "event": "High Surf Advisory",
          "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 15 at 3:43AM PST until November 17 at 4:00AM PST by NWS San Francisco CA",
          "severity": "Minor",
          "urgency": "Expected",
          "description": "* WHAT...Large breaking waves of 20 to 25 ft, with occasional sets\nof 25 to 35 ft at favored breakpoints.\n\n* WHERE...All Pacific Coast Beaches.\n\n* WHEN...Until 4 AM PST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...High tides will result in flooding of low-lying\ninfrastructure, isolated road closures, and coastal erosion.\nRising tides will bring water and waves farther up the beach\nthan normal, restricting escape from beaches and coastal areas.\nDangerously large breaking waves can overpower swimmers, pulling\npeople into the sea from beaches, jetties, and rocks resulting\nin significant physical injury and increasing the risk of\ndrowning. Waves can sweep across the shoreline without warning,\npulling people into the sea from beaches, jetties, and rocks.",
          "instruction": "Swimmers should remain out of the water due to dangerous surf\nconditions.",
          "expires": "2026-11-15T14:45:00-08:00",
